WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.151 --> 00:00:02.171
- Most of us call this our "Cookie Zone."

00:00:02.171 --> 00:00:05.352
(light holiday music)

00:00:05.352 --> 00:00:06.989
- International sweets are interesting.

00:00:06.989 --> 00:00:10.216
Some of them are gooey,
and drippy, and flaky.

00:00:10.216 --> 00:00:13.467
- I happen to have a particular
fondness for marzipan.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.678
- I personally like fruit.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.410
- So here we have a
jeera biscuit from India.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.514
- It looks almost like a ginger snap.

00:00:22.298 --> 00:00:22.859
- Hmm.

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:24.599
- Tastes like there's beans in it.

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:26.295
- Kind of reminds you of
those shortbread cookies

00:00:26.295 --> 00:00:27.235
a little bit.

00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:29.579
- Doesn't have a whole lot
of sugar, which is good.

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:31.518
- Tastes like corn meal.

00:00:31.518 --> 00:00:34.234
- There might be a little baking
soda or something in there.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.211
- It's flaky.

00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:37.717
- If you like that crumbly,

00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:40.133
crumb sensation in your mouth,

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:43.830
I guess someone might like that.

00:00:45.194 --> 00:00:47.214
- Looks like a nice little maple leaf.

00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:49.199
- Let's see what it tastes like.

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:50.511
- Tastes like maple.

00:00:50.511 --> 00:00:52.554
- Reminds me of little animal crackers

00:00:52.554 --> 00:00:54.179
that you might have had
when you were a kid.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:56.478
Not the frosted ones,
just the plain brown ones.

00:00:56.478 --> 00:00:58.553
- Crunchy, crumbly.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:03.055
It has a dramatic graham
cracker aftertaste.

00:01:03.055 --> 00:01:04.436
- Reminds me of when I was a kid

00:01:04.436 --> 00:01:07.883
and my mom used to mix up
peanut butter and honey

00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:09.733
and put it on bread for us.

00:01:09.733 --> 00:01:13.134
- We're going to take
just a little bit of it

00:01:13.134 --> 00:01:14.597
off like this.

00:01:14.597 --> 00:01:17.520
We're gong to place it
on the tip of my tongue.

00:01:18.372 --> 00:01:21.333
Almost a marzipan-y quality to it.

00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:22.604
- It's a dandy.

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.930
- The old Australian Tim Tam.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:26.776
- G'day mate.

00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:28.252
- G'day mates.

00:01:28.252 --> 00:01:29.830
This is Santa from down under.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.462
- Chocolate.

00:01:33.336 --> 00:01:35.089
It reminds me of making chocolate cake

00:01:35.089 --> 00:01:36.354
with my grandmother.

00:01:36.354 --> 00:01:37.330
- Nice crunch.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.070
- The chocolate taste
doesn't just jump out at you.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.354
It lies there in the
mouth saying, "Savor me."

00:01:43.354 --> 00:01:45.281
- You know, kind of sensual.

00:01:45.807 --> 00:01:47.247
- Superb aftertaste.

00:01:47.247 --> 00:01:49.494
- I'm going to have to
go to Australia again.

00:01:51.264 --> 00:01:52.250
- A bicho.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.463
- It has a density kind
of feel of a doughnut.

00:01:59.415 --> 00:02:02.405
It has a lot more chew
than I was expecting.

00:02:03.015 --> 00:02:04.755
- Mmm mmm mmm.

00:02:04.755 --> 00:02:06.276
- Big overgrown Twinky.

00:02:06.276 --> 00:02:08.656
Maybe it's Twinky's uncle.

00:02:08.656 --> 00:02:11.953
- It does have a real
eggy kind of a feel to it.

00:02:11.953 --> 00:02:13.775
- You know that you're going to enjoy it

00:02:13.775 --> 00:02:15.558
down to the last bite.

00:02:16.713 --> 00:02:18.048
- Well they were all delicious.

00:02:18.048 --> 00:02:20.776
- This Santa says, Bravo,

00:02:20.776 --> 00:02:23.586
and a big two thumbs up.

00:02:23.586 --> 00:02:26.325
- You've hit some unusual ones
here today, I'll tell you.

00:02:26.325 --> 00:02:27.927
- That's the beauty of the world,

00:02:27.927 --> 00:02:29.309
we all have our different cultures

00:02:29.309 --> 00:02:30.852
and we all have our different tastes.

00:02:30.852 --> 00:02:33.680
- But I love the graham cracker outside.

00:02:36.885 --> 00:02:39.221
- Santa said graham crapper. (laughs)

